<title>UK: Go-Ahead says trading meeting expectations.</title>
<headline>Go-Ahead says trading meeting expectations.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bus and train operator Go-Ahead Group Plc said on Tuesday that trading in the current year &quot;is well in line with expectations.&quot;</p>
<p>Chairman Sir Michael Straker told the company's annual meeting in Newcastle that the recent award of the Thames Trains franchise gave the company &quot;the credibility to win additional rail franchises in the UK&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;We are looking foward to exciting prospects in Europe as well,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Straker said the group's bus operations &quot;are running to target.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
